              "originalPosition": 31,
              "body": "Thanks for the look. I'd prefer to keep the active voice (\"report ...\")  since it matches the directive style used in the rest of this section's measurement procedures.\r\n\r\nIs your  goal was to separate the algo_factor-invariance point from the transfer-volume-reflects-keying point, I can do that with:\r\n\r\n>  When UET group keying is active during testing, reports MUST present the observed BusBW computed from measured bytes transferred. The algo_factor defined in {{!TERMINOLOGY}} (fixed per collective type) still applies to the BusBW formula; group keying affects only the observed transfer volume, not algo_factor.\r\n\r\nHappy to apply that variant if it addresses your concern \u2014 otherwise I'll leave the current text as-is.\r\n",
